From 8076ef67bc7d926e53b99205045d89cf4969cda3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lath <lath.solana@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:04:08 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] lath: fail loud on any config but the posture, and run
 with no shell

Under the lath feature a missing config is an error and nothing is written for it; an old schema, a section the resilient loader dropped, an unknown key or a config that does not validate stops the run instead of warning. The Lath posture check is an allow-list of the contract's keys and values: one custom provider, one agent with memory none, a non-empty allowed_tools within the eight, level full with no approvals, sandbox_enabled false, cost off, no retries, and the host-tool socket; any ZEROCLAW_* variable but NOW, OMIT_HOST and CONFIG_DIR, and a skills/ entry in the workspace, are refused by name. Skills load nothing, the open-skills clone and the skill HTTP tool are not compiled, skill creation and review never run, model_switch is out, create_runtime returns a shell-less adapter so no shell is resolved or stat'ed and the prompt has no Shell:, and create_sandbox detects nothing.
